# Verifier rules for the node/provider split of the 256-bit signers bitmap: bits [0, 64) are
# nodes and bits [64, 256) are provider signers. Every set bit counts toward `required`, at most
# one of them a provider bit. Every set bit names a live record; the aggregate key is the sum over
# all set bits. A registry stores two tables, nodes then providers: node slot i is nodes[i] (bit i),
# provider slot p is providers[p] (bit 64 + p), each table its segment's count long.
#
